FINDINGS (for antigravity chat A3; I report, I do not fix)

F1 (blocking under rule 15). Plant P4 is MISSED: DemandStore.export's
   status_filter has no test. test_export_to_directory (a0f450c) adds exactly one
   demand, never resolves or dismisses it, then asserts count == 1, which is the
   same answer with and without the filter. With the filter gone a resolved
   demand is exported under the header "Open Demands: 1". Fix in
   novacore/tests/test_demand.py: add a resolved entry and a dismissed entry,
   assert neither appears in DEMAND.md or demands.json while both are still
   readable through list(status="fulfilled" / "dismissed"). The product code is
   correct today; the gap is the test.

F2 (medium). tools/pack-shuttle.py defaults key_dir to out_dir / "test-keys", so
   a package built for a pendrive carries TEST-root.priv inside the folder the
   owner hands back. The seed is a public constant (TEST_KEY_SEED) and
   ShuttleImporter only trusts the key it is constructed with, so nothing is
   exposed unless the owner points the importer at TEST-root.pub; it is still the
   wrong shape to teach. Default key_dir outside out_dir and say so in --help.

F3 (low). The A3.11 schema guard is unreachable for a manifest that produced no
   failures, because verify_manifest's structure_errors rejects a manifest with
   no release or trust object first. It is defence in depth, and section 8 shows
   the test pins the message. Worth a comment saying so; no code change.

F4 (context, no action). The positive path is covered: a clean package writes a
   proposal, the store digest changes, and the proposal is applied=false with
   status proposed_unverified (oracle B). The no-sockets test covers /demand and
   the importer in-process: 5 tests, 0 socket events recorded.

VERDICT: FAIL
  My P1 (fails-closed guard), P2 (replay window) and P3 (payload hash) are all
  CAUGHT, which is the good outcome: those gates have teeth. P4 (the export
  status filter) is MISSED, so under rule 15 the item fails. The one blocking
  item is a test to add in A3's file; the production code is correct today.
